## Findings

- The map has **host rules only**, with no redirects and no path rules. Requests to the raw IP (Host = `136.68.140.144`) match no host rule, so they fall to the **default service `frontend-service`**. This is why `/ai-test/*` must be added at the **top level (`pathMatcher` for the default)**, not inside `path-matcher-1/2`.
- Staging traffic uses the PwC hostnames, so a rule that only matches the raw IP can't touch it. This keeps the risk low.

## Edit: add a host rule for the IP only

Create a new path matcher used only when Host = the IP. Staging hosts are untouched.

**Create the file** (run in Cloud Shell; copy-paste the whole block):

```bash
cat > url-map-new.yaml <<'EOF'
defaultService: https://www.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/pg-ae-n-app-125609/global/backendServices/frontend-service
fingerprint: bNmBHrRNKyY=
hostRules:
- hosts:
  - staging.careerdevelopmentnavigator.mer.pwc.com
  pathMatcher: path-matcher-1
- hosts:
  - stagingapi.careerdevelopmentnavigator.mer.pwc.com
  pathMatcher: path-matcher-2
- hosts:
  - 136.68.140.144
  pathMatcher: path-matcher-ai-test
name: cm-staging-lb
pathMatchers:
- defaultService: https://www.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/pg-ae-n-app-125609/global/backendServices/frontend-service
  name: path-matcher-1
- defaultService: https://www.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/pg-ae-n-app-125609/global/backendServices/app-backend-service
  name: path-matcher-2
- defaultService: https://www.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/pg-ae-n-app-125609/global/backendServices/frontend-service
  name: path-matcher-ai-test
  routeRules:
  - priority: 1
    matchRules:
    - prefixMatch: /ai-test/
    service: https://www.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/pg-ae-n-app-125609/global/backendServices/ai-test-backend
    routeAction:
      urlRewrite:
        pathPrefixRewrite: /
EOF
```

**⚠️ Prerequisite:** `ai-test-backend` must exist first (the import fails otherwise). Confirm with:
```bash
gcloud compute backend-services describe ai-test-backend --global --format="value(name)"
```

**Apply:**
```bash
gcloud compute url-maps validate --source=url-map-new.yaml --global
gcloud compute url-maps import cm-staging-lb --global --source=url-map-new.yaml
```
If the fingerprint is rejected (map changed), re-export and re-apply the edit. Don't use `--quiet`.

## Verify
```bash
gcloud compute backend-services get-health ai-test-backend --global
curl -i http://136.68.140.144/ai-test/health
curl -sI http://136.68.140.144/
```
Expected: `HEALTHY`, a 200 with `{"status":"healthy"}`, and `/` still served by the default `frontend-service`. Wait 2-5 minutes after the import for propagation.

Note: `/ai-test` without the trailing slash falls through to `frontend-service`. Always use `/ai-test/...`.

